blocks.text:
Isay ek tasveer ki tarah samjhiye. Sandwich ka naam yahin se aaya: neeche roti (bread) \(f\), oopar roti \(h\), aur beech mein bharti (filling) \(g\). Jab \(x\) number \(c\) ke qareeb aata hai to neeche wali roti bhi \(L\) ki taraf jati hai aur oopar wali bhi \(L\) ki taraf. Dono rotiyan aapas mein dab jati hain, to beech wali bharti bhi \(L\) par hi pahunchegi. Yahi theorem ka saara matlab hai.
Ek aur misaal roz marra ki: agar aap do doston ke beech chal rahe hain aur dono dost ek hi darwaze mein daakhil ho rahe hain, aur aap hamesha un dono ke beech hain, to aap bhi usi darwaze mein daakhil honge.
Teen sharaait (conditions) yaad rakhiye, teeno zaroori hain:
1. \(c\) ke aas paas har \(x\) ke liye \(f(x) \le g(x) \le h(x)\) (khud \(c\) par kya hota hai, is se farq nahin parta);
2. \(\lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L\);
3. \(\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = L\), aur yeh wahi \(L\) hona chahiye.
